report: "---\nauthor: \"builder\"\ncreated: \"2026-11-23\"\nupdated: \"2026-11-23\"\n---\n\n# Pin the XS oracle's Math to libm 0.2.16 (soft floats)\n\nJob `ironhorse-xs-oracle-pinned-libm`, project `endojs/endo-but-for-bots`.\nBranch `job/ironhorse-xs-oracle-pinned-libm/2` in the project checkout. It starts\nfrom `fix/xs-oracle-pinned-libm`, whose WIP commit I split and finished. Base is\n`036876777` on `llm`.\n\n## Commits\n\n```\n018d98a85 chore: Update Cargo.lock\na386f5ebc fix(xs-oracle): pin the oracle's Math to libm 0.2.16 soft floats\n983d1b067 fix(ironhorse-262): compare a deterministic-math Ironhorse with the pinned oracle\nf019eb34e test(ironhorse): record stage3-math 055 and 057 from the pinned oracle\n7c987fe40 docs(ironhorse): record that the XS oracle uses the pinned Math provider\n```\n\nPackages touched: `rust/engine/xs-oracle`, `rust/engine/ironhorse-262`,\n`rust/engine/ironhorse-fuzz` (manifest only), `rust/engine/ironhorse-vm` (one test\nand its fixture), `packages/test262-runner` (two converted cases), `.github/workflows/ci.yml`,\n`rust/engine/DETERMINISM-METERING.md`.\n\n## What changed\n\n1. **The build (step 1).** The WIP's E0463 came from this box, not from the\n   change. The toolchain at `/opt/garden/cap` has only the musl `std`, and there is\n   no C compiler. I installed Rust 1.91.1 through rustup into the slot home, used\n   `zig cc` as `cc`, and fetched the pinned Moddable commit `23b4d6b0a65f` as a\n   source archive into `c/moddable` (the garden holds no mirror of it, and it is not\n   committed). After that, `cargo build --locked -p xs-oracle` passes. The WIP's\n   Cargo.lock line was already correct (`--locked` accepts it). Its own commit\n   follows AGENTS.md's lockfile rule, which the history applies to Cargo.lock too.\n2. **The oracle pin** works as the WIP designed it. `build.rs` defines the 22\n   provider-sensitive `c_*` macros of `xsPlatform.h` to `xsoracle_*` functions in\n   `src/math.rs`, which call `libm =0.2.16` with `force-soft-floats`. New test\n   `xs-oracle/tests/pinned_math.rs` runs all 22 operations plus `**` on XS and\n   requires libm's exact bits. **Seen to fail without the change:** with the\n   `build.define` loop disabled, it fails on this glibc host for `acosh(2.3)`\n   (XS `3ff799c88e79140d`, libm `…0c`), `exp(1)` (`4005bf0a8b145769` against `…6a`) and\n   `tanh(0.3)` (`3fd2a4dda7d914fa` against `…f9`). Restored, it passes.\n3. **The Ironhorse side (step 2).** `ironhorse-262` and `ironhorse-fuzz`, the two\n   dual-run harnesses, now depend on `ironhorse-vm` with `deterministic-math`.\n   I chose this over a CLI flag because the comparison is only meaningful with one\n   provider on both sides: a plain local `cargo test -p ironhorse-262` should not\n   compare platform Ironhorse against a pinned oracle. Feature selection, checked with\n   `cargo tree -e features -i ironhorse-vm`:\n   - Deterministic: `-p ironhorse-262`, `--workspace`, and the oracle lane's test\n     invocation (`-p ironhorse-compile -p ironhorse-regexp -p ironhorse-262 -p ironhorse-fuzz --features …/parity`).\n     The corpus gates (`cargo run -p ironhorse-262 --bin endot-ih`) and the sanitizer\n     script (same package set) are deterministic too.\n   - Platform, unchanged: the `test-ironhorse` lane's invocation\n     (`-p ironhorse-runtime … -p ironhorse-regexp --features ironhorse-vm/store-integrity`),\n     its platform Math vector exports, and the SES realm-profile step\n     (`-p ironhorse-vm --test ses_* --features …/parity`).\n   - Cost: the oracle lane's `--workspace` `-D warnings` build and Clippy no longer\n     compile the platform arm of `ironhorse-vm/src/math.rs`. A new step in that lane\n     runs `cargo +1.88.0 clippy --locked -p ironhorse-vm --no-deps -- -D warnings`\n     so the platform arm keeps its lint gate.\n4. **Expectation changes (step 3).** Two values changed, nothing else:\n   - `stage3-math/055.js` `Math.acosh(2.3)`: old `3ff799c88e79140d` (1.4750447812414251),\n     new `3ff799c88e79140c` (1.475044781241425).\n   - `stage3-math/057.js` `Math.exp(1)`: old `4005bf0a8b145769` (2.718281828459045),\n     new `4005bf0a8b14576a` (2.7182818284590455).\n\n   These cases assert the oracle's completion as recorded by `corpus-to-262`. The\n   corpora are retired, so I took the new values from the pinned oracle's\n   `String()` output and wrote them in by hand. Without this change, both engines\n   fail the old assertion the same way, and `corpus_conversion_equivalence` covers\n   1709 of 1711. I updated the values rather than accept two named skips, which\n   would have lowered that floor. **This is a judgment call for the maintainer:**\n   the new values are each one ULP from the correctly rounded result\n   (`Math.exp(1) !== Math.E` under the pinned provider). If you would rather keep\n   the old assertions, drop `f019eb34e`, and the two cases need a different home.\n   `math_corpus_profile`'s C7 inventory flips to match: all 30 pass under\n   deterministic Math, and the platform arm's two divergences are now recorded in\n   `tests/fixtures/math-corpus-platform.tsv` (renamed from `math-corpus-libm.tsv`).\n   No floor was lowered. The `ironhorse.txt` and `try.txt` expectation lists are\n   unchanged. No snapshot golden changed: `ironhorse-snapshot`'s tests (which\n   keep separate goldens for each provider) run only in invocations whose\n   feature selection this change leaves alone.\n5. **Docs (step 4).** The C7 section of `DETERMINISM-METERING.md` now records the\n   maintainer's reversal, the feature selection, and the two changed values. There\n   is no `ubuntu-24.04` pin to drop: PR #1613's runner pin is not on this branch,\n   and both oracle lanes run on `ubuntu-latest`. With this change, #1613 is no\n   longer needed for these lanes.\n\n## What I ran (Rust 1.91.1 unless noted, Debian 13 x86_64, glibc)\n\n- `cargo build --locked -p xs-oracle`: passes.\n- `cargo test --locked -p xs-oracle --test pinned_math`: passes, and fails with the\n  redirection disabled (above).\n- The oracle lane's command as CI runs it, with `--no-fail-fast`,\n  `RUST_MIN_STACK=33554432`, `TEST262_DIR` at the pinned `be13516f…` checkout and\n  `IRONHORSE_COMPILER_TOTALITY_REQUIRED=1`: 1898 passed, 3 failed, 17 ignored,\n  before the fixture commit. The compiler totality test ran over the corpus\n  (155 s) and passed. The three failures:\n  - `corpus_conversion_equivalence`: 1709 of 1711, the two cases above. After\n    `f019eb34e` it passes.\n  - `expectation_shards::complete_reports_retain_failed_ratchets_across_resume_and_quarantine`:\n    caused by this box. `/tmp` is noexec, so the test's stub `cargo` cannot run.\n    It passes with `TMPDIR` on an executable filesystem.\n  - `ironhorse-fuzz` `seeds::tests::the_checked_in_seed_corpus_is_current`:\n    **predates this change.** It also fails with `ironhorse-fuzz`'s base manifest\n    (platform Math), and `write-seed-corpus` produces byte-identical seeds under\n    both providers. The `snapshot_roundtrip`, `snapshot_decoder` and\n    `store_decoder` seeds are stale on this host. I left them alone; regenerating\n    them is a separate change, if CI shows the same.\n- `cargo test -p ironhorse-vm --test math_corpus_profile`, platform and\n  `--features deterministic-math`: both pass.\n- Gate: `endot-ih --direct-only --strict-skip-reasons --expectations ironhorse-262/expectations/try.txt language/statements/try`:\n  expectations met, 99 covered.\n- Gate: `endot-ih --strict-skip-reasons --repeat 3 --expectations ironhorse-262/expectations/ironhorse.txt ../../packages/test262-runner/test262/test/ironhorse`:\n  expectations met, 1712 of 1712 covered. With the old 055/057 values it fails:\n  `REGRESSION … 055.js [sloppy] pass -> shared-test262-failure`, and the same for 057.\n  Before this change, the lanes on 26.04 reported 054/055 as over-acceptance\n  (per the job); here every stage3-math case passes on both sides.\n- Rust 1.88.0, as the oracle lane runs it: `RUSTFLAGS=-D warnings cargo build --locked --workspace`,\n  `cargo clippy --locked --workspace --no-deps -- -D warnings`, and the new\n  `cargo clippy --locked -p ironhorse-vm --no-deps -- -D warnings`: all pass.\n- `cargo fmt -p xs-oracle -- --check`: passes. `garden prose diff 036876777`: clean.\n\nNot run: the sanitizer lane (needs clang with the ASan and UBSan runtimes), the SES\nartifact steps (they need the generated bundles and are unaffected), the\n`test-ironhorse` lane (its feature selection is unchanged), and macOS.\n\n## Proposed pull request\n\nTitle: `fix(xs-oracle): pin the oracle's Math to libm 0.2.16 soft floats`\n\nBody:\n\n> The oracle lanes (`test-ironhorse-oracle`, `ironhorse-oracle-sanitizers`) are red\n> because `ubuntu-latest` became 26.04, whose glibc rounds `asinh`/`acosh`\n> correctly; the XS oracle linked the host libm, so stage3-math 054/055 moved by one\n> ULP. Per the maintainer (\"Let's pin libm. We want determinism for a particular\n> binary and do not require it beyond that.\"), this replaces #1613's runner pin with\n> a pin in source.\n>\n> - xs-oracle: the 22 provider-sensitive `c_*` macros of XS's platform layer now call\n>   libm 0.2.16 (soft floats), the provider `ironhorse-vm` uses under\n>   `deterministic-math`. A test requires libm's exact bits from XS.\n> - ironhorse-262 and ironhorse-fuzz enable `ironhorse-vm/deterministic-math`, so both\n>   sides of every dual-run comparison use one provider. The `test-ironhorse` lane\n>   still tests the platform configuration; a new oracle-lane step lints it.\n> - stage3-math 055 (`acosh(2.3)`) and 057 (`exp(1)`) now assert the pinned oracle's\n>   result, one ULP from the previous platform value; the C7 inventory now records\n>   the platform provider's divergences instead.\n> - DETERMINISM-METERING.md records the reversal of C7's \"oracle keeps its platform\n>   provider\".\n>\n> Supersedes #1613 for these lanes.\n\nOpen it as a draft. Review is a separate job; I did not review my own work.\n\n## What is left\n\n- The maintainer's call on the 055/057 values (above).\n- The stale fuzz seed corpus, if CI shows the same failure on `llm`.\n- CI confirmation on Linux and macOS, and the sanitizer lane.\n"
